title start
kind: default
tags: comment todo
Comments and todo marks on blocks
title end

paragraph start
This page shows two features. A comment can be attached to one block or to several blocks at once. A todo mark puts the word TODO down the left edge of any block.
paragraph end

section start
title start
A comment on one block
title end

paragraph start
Install the tool on a clean machine and run the checker on one page.
comment start
This comment sits inside the paragraph it belongs to. The viewer draws it as its own box inside that block, so you see at once what it is about.
comment end
paragraph end
section end

section start
title start
A comment on two blocks
title end

comment start
One comment for both paragraphs below. Write the note first, then put the blocks it covers inside the comment.

paragraph start
First block covered by the comment.
paragraph end

paragraph start
Second block covered by the same comment.
paragraph end
comment end
section end

section start
title start
A todo mark
title end

paragraph start
todo: write the install guide and test it on a clean machine before Friday
Install the tool on a clean machine and run the checker on one page.
comment start
The word todo, a colon and a description under the start line puts TODO in the top-right corner and hangs the description under the box. Start the description with done when the task is finished.
comment end
paragraph end

paragraph start
todo: done viewer fixed, names now sit on the left
Fix the viewer so block names sit on the left.
paragraph end
section end
